  "articleBody": "Basic shelving is an easy weekend chore, but complete garage finishing involves structural, safety, and mechanical considerations that demand general contractor oversight.\n\nKey indicators that professional help is needed:\n- You need dedicated electrical circuits for heavy power tools, electric vehicle chargers, or specialized lighting.\n- The shared wall with your home requires proper fire-rated assemblies and sealed air barriers.\n- Your walls show signs of settling, water seepage, or damaged framing that needs repair before closing up.\n- You want seamless drywall finishing, texture, and trim carpentry that matches the rest of your home's quality.\n- The ceiling requires attic access framing, structural reinforcement, or high R-value insulation installation.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps: An experienced contractor coordinates electrical sub-trades while personally handling carpentry, drywall hanging, taping, and interior painting to deliver a clean, durable space.\n\nLooking to finish your garage walls, lighting, and trim? Contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to review your interior finishing project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}